The "exec" case has a borrow issue: `let begin = match &arg(3) { V::Str(s) => Some(s.s.as_str()), _ => None };` — `arg(3)` returns a temporary V. In the "run" case it worked because... wait, "run" has the same pattern:

```rust
let begin_arg = arg(3);
let begin = match &begin_arg {
    V::Str(s) => Some(s.s.as_str()),
    _ => None,
};
```

"run" binds `begin_arg` first. My "exec"/"dml" used `match &arg(3)` directly. Fix by binding first.

